Changes made:

**`src/types.ts:4`** — Added `"storehouse"` to the `BuildingKind` union:
```ts
export type BuildingKind = "hut" | "farm" | "quarry" | "storehouse";
```

**`src/sim.ts`**
- Added the storehouse cost to `BUILDING_COSTS` (`{ wood: 25, stone: 10 }`).
- Added a new `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` map. Kinds with no prerequisite are simply omitted (so hut/farm/quarry need nothing), and `storehouse` requires `["hut"]`:
```ts
export const BUILDING_PREREQUISITES: Partial<Record<BuildingKind, BuildingKind[]>> = {
  storehouse: ["hut"],
};
```
- Implemented `availableBuildings`:
```ts
export function availableBuildings(settlement: Settlement): BuildingKind[] {
  return (Object.keys(BUILDING_COSTS) as BuildingKind[]).filter((kind) => {
    if (!canAfford(settlement, kind)) {
      return false;
    }
    const prerequisites = BUILDING_PREREQUISITES[kind];
    if (!prerequisites) {
      return true;
    }
    return prerequisites.every((prereq) => settlement.buildings.includes(prereq));
  });
}
```

Behavior verified:
- Empty settlement → `["hut", "farm", "quarry"]` (storehouse hidden — no hut).
- With a built hut + enough resources → storehouse included.
- Storehouse hidden when no hut exists even with ample resources.
- Storehouse hidden when unaffordable (e.g. wood 24 < 25) even with a hut.

The design keeps the no-prerequisite kinds as a plain omission in the map, matching the existing data-driven style, and `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` is exported so it stays easy to extend.


